[[0,527513,0,6,0,6,"2015-09-20T15:48:25","jpw42","",[],"","UPDATED: High-Speed Chase Ends In Crash Outside Blooming Prairie Elementary School | Steele County Times and News Enterprise","http://www.bloomingprairieonline.com/news/updated-high-speed-chase-ends-crash-outside-blooming-prairie-elementary-school","news"],[1,2514843,0,2,0,2,"2015-09-20T16:27:54","MarcoVincenzo","",[],"<blockquote>\n<p>The incident began around 7:30 a.m. with a traffic stop for a seatbelt violation</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I've no idea why this guy got so upset over such a minor issue. But, the cops certainly shouldn't even begin a &quot;high speed pursuit&quot; for such a piddly &quot;crime&quot;. How many peoples' lives did they endanger to catch a guy not wearing a seatbelt?</p>"],[2,2515063,2514843,0,0,0,"2015-09-20T16:49:36","goodluvin","[e]",[],"<p>He is just a little unstable. What if he was highly intoxicated? \n</p>\n<p>Cops did a great job. The construction worker did a better one. </p>"],[2,2515454,2514843,0,0,0,"2015-09-20T17:23:21","jpw42","",[],"<p>I kinda agree with you on this. The place where I differ is Seat-belt violation should not be a crime. But so long as it is you have to pursue. </p>"],[3,2515536,2515454,1,0,1,"2015-09-20T17:31:32","MarcoVincenzo","",[],"<p>Cops can always choose not to pursue. Pursuits are dangerous so they have that flexibility. Now, if they're going after someone who is dangerous then the choice is obvious. But, they had this guys name and knew everything about him and his only &quot;crime&quot; was not wearing a seatbelt--he wasn't dangerous. Let him go, and then go arrest him at home later without endangering others. This incident was simply a bunch of power hungry cops not thinking about the consequences of their actions.</p>"],[4,2516852,2515536,0,0,0,"2015-09-20T19:28:21","jpw42","",[],"<p>You say</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>his only &quot;crime&quot; was not wearing a seatbelt</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The Steele County Times states </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Castilleja got back in the vehicle, put it in reverse, hit the deputy’s vehicle and then sped off.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Pretty sure it is a crime to ram a squad car. Also a crime to flee from the police. </p>"]]
